{# =========================================================================
   WAD list
   Every WAD the plugin can see, with its name and which one loads by default.

   Its own file because the settings screen swaps it in place after a download
   rather than reloading: the page is a form with data-confirm-unload on it, so
   a reload mid-edit either loses names the admin has typed or stops to ask
   about them.

   Rendered on its own by daemon/wad/list, which has to re-apply the `settings`
   namespace Craft wraps plugin settings in. Without that the inputs come back
   named wadNames[...] rather than settings[wadNames][...] and saving quietly
   stops persisting anything they hold.
   ========================================================================= #}

{% import '_includes/forms.twig' as forms %}

{% if available %}
    <p class="light">{{ 'Everything the plugin can see. The default is what loads when you open the Daemon screen, and the game dropdown in the breadcrumbs switches between them. Leave a name empty to use the one shown.'|t('daemon') }}</p>

    {# Craft's editable table markup, written out rather than built with
       forms.editableTableField.

       The component keys its cells as name[rowId][colId], which would turn a
       flat map of names into a map of single-key maps, and it takes one
       placeholder per column. Both matter here: the rows are files on disk
       rather than rows a person adds, and each one needs its own placeholder,
       because the placeholder is the name the plugin would pick on its own.

       No Craft.EditableTable is initialised. Its job is adding, deleting and
       reordering rows, and none of that applies to a list the filesystem
       decides. #}
    <table id="daemon-wad-names" class="editable fullwidth daemon-wad-table">
        <col>
        <col class="daemon-col-name">
        <col>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th id="daemon-wad-names-default" scope="col" class="checkbox-cell thin">{{ 'Default'|t('daemon') }}</th>
                <th id="daemon-wad-names-name" scope="col" class="singleline-cell textual daemon-name-cell">{{ 'Name'|t('daemon') }}</th>
                <th id="daemon-wad-names-file" scope="col" class="heading-cell">{{ 'File'|t('daemon') }}</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for wad in available %}
                <tr>
                    {# Checked off the list order rather than off the setting.
                       The service sorts the chosen default first, so the first
                       row is the effective default whether or not one was ever
                       picked, and the control shows what is actually happening
                       rather than what was last saved. #}
                    <td class="checkbox-cell thin">
                        {{ forms.radio({
                            id: 'defaultWad-' ~ wad.key,
                            name: 'defaultWad',
                            value: wad.key,
                            checked: loop.first,
                            label: 'Load {name} by default'|t('daemon', {name: wad.name}),
                            containerAttributes: {class: 'visually-hidden'},
                        }) }}
                    </td>
                    <td class="singleline-cell textual daemon-name-cell">
                        {{ tag('textarea', {
                            name: 'wadNames[' ~ wad.key ~ ']',
                            rows: 1,
                            placeholder: wad.defaultName,
                            text: settings.wadNames[wad.key] ?? '',
                            aria: {labelledby: 'daemon-wad-names-name'},
                        }) }}
                    </td>
                    {# The path is the row's header: it is what identifies the
                       row, so a screen reader reading the name field announces
                       which file it belongs to. #}
                    <th scope="row" class="heading-cell">
                        <code>{{ wad.path }}</code>
                    </th>
                </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>
{% else %}
    <p class="light">
        {{ 'No WADs found yet. Freedoom is a free, BSD licensed replacement for the id WADs, and it is all this needs to run.'|t('daemon') }}
    </p>
{% endif %}
